WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.950
In this post-Endgame world, the Thor series
is breaking new ground for Marvel as The Odinson

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.780
becomes the first hero to be granted four
solo films.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:12.080
Thanks to a ton of new details spewing from
the hype factory that is San Diego Comic-Con,

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.200
we know a little more about what to expect
from the upcoming Thor 4.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.439
If you're a little behind on your Thor lore,
let's get you up to speed.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.940
In 2017, under the direction of Taika Waititi,
Ragnarok sprung into theaters.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:28.069
The movie chronicled Thor's attempts to save
Asgard from his conniving and powerful sister

00:00:28.069 --> 00:00:32.230
Hela — along with his struggle to escape
from the garbage planet Sakaar with Loki and

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:32.820
Bruce Banner.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.620
By introducing new characters like Valkyrie
— along with everybody's favorite alien

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.800
bros Korg and Miek …

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.120
"Hey man.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:41.460
I'm Korg.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.160
This is Miek.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.200
We're gonna jump on that spaceship and get
outta here.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:44.880
Wanna come?"

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.660
… and injecting a much-needed dose of whimsy
into the Thor series, Ragnarok became a welcome

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:53.820
addition to the MCU, receiving rave reviews
and crushing the box office.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.360
Ragnarok finds Thor learning to accept that,
as Odin and Heimdall said …

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.480
"Asgard is not a place — it's a people."

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:07.040
Recognizing that the only way to save his
home is to let it be destroyed, he finally

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:11.130
takes his place as king as he shepherds his
citizens into space, charting a course for

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.040
a new home on Earth.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:16.460
Tragically, that's where Thanos comes in,
leaving half of the Asgardian refugees dead

00:01:16.469 --> 00:01:19.670
in his quest for the Infinity Stones as Avengers:
Infinity War begins.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:24.729
A devastated Thor survives Thanos' final snap,
leaving him to spend Endgame seeking justice

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:26.130
and revenge for those he's lost.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:30.440
When Thanos is at last defeated, Thor is one
of the only original Avengers left standing.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:34.220
Ultimately, he ends up joining the Guardians
of the Galaxy to fight evil throughout the

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:38.450
universe, leaving his right-hand woman, Valkyrie,
in charge of the recently-founded Norwegian

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.820
territory of New Asgard.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.100
All of this has set the stage for what's to
come in the next Thor movie.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:48.140
After the success of Thor: Ragnarok, it makes
sense that Marvel would want director Taika

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:52.560
Waititi to return for Thor 4, considering
the acclaim that Waititi's irreverent and

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.060
dry comedic sensibilities garnered for Ragnarok.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:59.420
By taking one of Marvel's most serious and
austere superheroes and making him and his

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:03.640
surrounding cast totally accessible and even
fun, Waititi immediately left a mark on the

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:07.330
franchise and made himself indispensable as
a fresh voice in the MCU.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:11.820
"This one time when we were children, he transformed
himself into a snake and he knows that I love

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:15.250
snakes, so then I went to pick up the snake
to admire it, and he transformed back into

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.290
himself and went 'MYEH!

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:16.780
It's me!'

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:21.092
Even though Marvel fans are likely thrilled
that Waititi is officially confirmed to return

00:02:21.092 --> 00:02:25.860
for the fourth Thor film, it does get in the
way of one of his other long-awaited projects.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.110
Waititi is placing his adaptation of the cyberpunk
anime classic Akira on hold so that he can

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:34.450
return to the MCU, despite the fact that the
project had recently been fast-tracked by

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:35.000
Warner Bros.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.400
Fans can only hope that Waititi will be able
to revive Akira after he completes Thor 4,

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.760
but it's still clear that the filmmaker is
giving up plenty of opportunities to make

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.880
sure he can return to the Marvel cosmos.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:50.620
It's usually a safe bet that Marvel will have
a strong showing at San Diego Comic-Con, and

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:54.930
in 2019, as the studio looked forward post-Phase
3, there was plenty of breaking news about

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:57.800
upcoming Marvel projects, including Thor's
next outing.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:02.500
During the huge Marvel panel on Saturday,
July 20th at SDCC, cast members — along

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:06.780
with Waititi himself — made an appearance
to make a few major announcements about Thor

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:07.280
4.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.120
First off, the film's official title will
be Thor: Love and Thunder, which could give

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.810
us some indication about the film's tone as
well as tell us a little about what lies in

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:18.600
store for Thor himself — maybe the hero
will be able to find a little time for romance

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.620
between fights with various bad guys.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:24.700
As far as the release date goes, Thor: Love
and Thunder will hit theaters on November

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:28.560
5th, 2021, serving as the finale of the MCU's
Phase 4.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:33.200
A fourth Thor movie likely wouldn't have even
gotten a greenlight if Chris Hemsworth hadn't

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.880
hopped back on board to play what has now
become his signature role, so it's not surprising

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.060
that he is expected to return as the God of
Thunder.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.880
Though Hemsworth's Thor was a bit too serious
in the earlier films, Ragnarok and Endgame

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.080
both saw a sillier side of the superhero.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:49.300
In Ragnarok, during his time as a captive
of Jeff Goldblum's ridiculous Grandmaster,

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.060
he ends up slated to fight the Hulk, leading
to one of the film's most infamous lines.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.000
"Hey!

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:54.880
Hey!

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:56.720
We know each other!

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.300
He's a friend from work!"

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:03.100
Even as he tries to save his ancestral home
from Hela's clutches, he maintains a healthy

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:03.960
sense of humor.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:08.020
Endgame sees Thor returning to his serious
roots as he mourns the victims of Thanos,

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:12.230
but he still gets plenty of comedic moments
when his fellow Avengers discover "Bro Thor"

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.980
five years after the team parts ways.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:17.200
"No, no — give me that."

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:18.620
“You have the little one."

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:24.400
Serving as an unexpectedly comedic presence
in such a heavy film, Hemsworth anchors his

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.419
emotional beats while still keeping his performance
light and entertaining, proving that he's

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:32.159
more than capable of playing Thor in Love
and Thunder and for years to come.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.240
"Are you crying?"

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.180
"No….. yes."

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:41.900
Quite a few familiar faces will return for
Thor: Love and Thunder, including one Oscar

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.620
winner who's been absent from the film series
for a while now.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:49.150
In an unsurprising bit of news that was also
announced at SDCC, Tessa Thompson will return

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:53.361
to play the fierce, swaggering Valkyrie, who's
currently handling matters in New Asgard during

00:04:53.361 --> 00:04:56.260
Thor's post-Endgame jaunt with the Guardians
of the Galaxy.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:00.680
Thompson and head Marvel honcho Kevin Feige
also made it clear that the movie would confirm

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:05.310
Valkyrie's bisexuality, noting that she needs
to "find her queen," making for a landmark

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:08.880
in representation and diversity in this multi-franchise
universe.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.680
However, the most exciting casting announcement
was undoubtedly that Natalie Portman, who

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:16.770
played Thor's love interest Jane in both Thor
and Thor: The Dark World, will return to the

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:20.909
franchise and pick up Mjolnir herself as a
new Thor — just as the character did in

00:05:20.909 --> 00:05:23.370
a recent comics run from writer Jason Aaron.

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:27.460
As Portman took the stage and held Mjolnir
high to celebrate this thrilling development,

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:30.260
she quipped, quote, "I've always had a little
hammer envy."

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:34.220
The talented actress' return to the world
of Thor would have been big enough news, but

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:37.460
letting Portman become a superhero in her
own right just ups the ante.

